.TH PARDUS-IP-CONFLICT-NOTIFIER 1 "October 2026" "pardus-ip-conflict-notifier" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pardus-ip-conflict-notifier \- desktop notification for IP address conflicts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pardus-ip-conflict-notifier
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RB [ \-\-broadcast ]
.B \-\-title
.I title
.B \-\-message
.I message
.br
.B pardus-ip-conflict-notifier
.BR \-\-version | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pardus-ip-conflict-notifier
shows a desktop notification when
.BR ipwatchd (8)
detects an IPv4 address conflict.
.PP
It is a drop-in replacement for
.BR ipwatchd-gnotify ,
which is installed as a symbolic link to this program.
The default
.BR ipwatchd-script (1)
already calls
.BR /usr/sbin/ipwatchd-gnotify ,
so no configuration is needed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ipwatchd (root)
  -> /usr/sbin/ipwatchd-script "dev" "ip" "mac"
    -> /usr/sbin/ipwatchd-gnotify --broadcast ...
      -> notification for every local graphical user
.fi
.RE
.PP
When the message has the format produced by
.BR ipwatchd-script ,
the notification is shown in the system language with the IP address,
interface and hardware address of the conflicting device.
Any other message is shown as given.
.PP
Desktop users need no extra privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Print the sessions found and the commands run to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-broadcast
Send the notification to every local X11 or Wayland session reported by
.BR loginctl (1),
once per user. Requires root privileges.
Without this option the notification is shown only in the caller's own session.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title " " \fItitle\fR
Title of the notification.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message " " \fImessage\fR
Text of the notification.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help message and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The notification was sent to every target session.
.TP
.B 1
At least one notification could not be sent, or
.B \-\-broadcast
was used without root privileges.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Test the whole notification path as ipwatchd would run it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo /usr/sbin/ipwatchd-gnotify --debug --broadcast \e
    --title "IP conflict occurred" \e
    --message "MAC address 8:0:27:1:2:3 causes IP conflict with address 10.0.2.15 set on interface enp0s3"
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
Only conflicts detected by
.BR ipwatchd (8)
at runtime are reported. A conflict detected by NetworkManager while
activating a connection, where the address is never configured, is not
visible to ipwatchd.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ipwatchd (8),
.BR ipwatchd.conf (5),
.BR ipwatchd-script (1),
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR loginctl (1)
